                        "I/O and mutation checks prove that missing, unreadable, directory, interrupted-read, and unexpected read failures disclose neither paths nor host messages and yield the stable `io-error`; repeated execution is independent of locale, timezone, current date, network, and environment variables. For the same readable operand bytes and effective readability, unrelated directory activity, metadata changes that do not affect access, and replacement or mutation elsewhere do not change observable behavior. If the explicit operand changes while being read, checks prove that the CLI applies its contract to the actual bytes obtained by one complete read: valid complete bytes produce their weekday counts, invalid complete bytes produce the corresponding deterministic validation failure, and mutation that prevents or interrupts a complete read or makes the operand inaccessible produces `io-error`. No check requires snapshot isolation, locking, retries, or preservation of a result for bytes that existed before mutation."
                      ],
                      "scope": [
                        "A deterministic bounded CLI named `iso-date-weekday`.",
                        "Exactly one explicit regular UTF-8 file containing one canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` record per line and at least one date.",
                        "Proleptic-Gregorian years `0001` through `9999`, with civil-date-only weekday computation.",
                        "Compact JSON counts ordered Monday through Sunday, with atomic fail-closed validation and stable automation output.",
                        "A PUBLIC, initially empty pilot target at `https://github.com/taylorrowser/mdlm-iso-date-weekday-pilot`."
